### Prioritized Remediation Plan

| Priority | Smell | Fix Effort | Impact |
|----------|-------|-----------|--------|
| 1 | Assertion-Free Test | ~2 min | Eliminates false-pass risk |
| 2 | Conditional Test Logic | ~5 min | Uncovers hidden untested branch |
| 3 | Sleepy Test | ~3 min | Speeds suite by 2s, removes flakiness |
| 4 | Mystery Guest | ~3 min | Makes test portable and self-contained |
| 5 | Exception Handling | ~2 min | Modernize to `Assert.ThrowsException` |
| 6 | Magic Number Test | ~5 min | Makes intent self-documenting |
| 7 | Sensitive Equality | ~5 min | Decouples from display format |
| 8 | Eager Test | ~10 min | Improves failure diagnosis (or tag as integration) |
| 9 | General Fixture | ~1 min | Remove unused `_logger` field |

**Bottom line:** 8 of 9 tests carry at least one academic test smell. The single clean test (`ValidateOrder_NullOrder_ThrowsArgumentNullException`) demonstrates the pattern the rest should follow. Start with the High-severity findings — they directly risk false passes or flaky failures.
